+#: Why the integration line must not carry an earlier run's prerequisite
+#: (:func:`_prereqs_to_carry`) — each one holds the dependents that would build on it: no
+#: branch on record (nothing of it to fold); a record older than its latest sign-off (the
+#: branch may be a rejected attempt's); a PR closed without merging (rejected work, in no
+#: base); no PR on record, or a host that did not answer (whether the base already has its
+#: work is not known).
+_UNPUBLISHED, _STALE, _CLOSED, _NO_PR, _UNREAD = (
+    "unpublished", "stale", "closed", "no-pr", "unread")
+_HOLDS = frozenset((_UNPUBLISHED, _STALE, _CLOSED, _NO_PR, _UNREAD))
+#: ... and the two verdicts that hold nothing: carry it on the line, or it is the base.
+_CARRY, _BASE = "carry", "base"
+
+
+def _prereqs_to_carry(cfg: Config, bundles: list[Path], batch_names: set[str], *, dry: bool,
+                      ) -> tuple[list[Path], dict[str, tuple[str, list[str]]]]:
+    """The earlier runs' prerequisites a stack-mode run must carry on its integration line
+    before wave 0, and the dependents it must hold instead (#616).
+
+    A prerequisite outside the batch is COMPLETE, which means only that its draft PR was
+    opened: until that PR merges its work is in no base, and only the line can carry it.
+    Only a plain ``Depends on`` edge of a drive-set bundle starts a line. A ``Depends on
+    (merged)`` one keeps its #186 gate in :func:`_runnable` and waits for the merge. A
+    legacy ``Stacks on`` one (#123) starts none: with no line on its target its bundle
+    builds on the parent's own branch (and, own-repo, opens its PR against it), as it
+    always has. A line THIS fold starts has every bundle of its target built on it, so it
+    carries their ``Stacks on`` parents too, judged like ``Depends on`` ones. Only that
+    line: one first folded after a later wave (an in-batch prerequisite's) carries no
+    earlier run's ``Stacks on`` parent, so a bundle stacking on one and pointed at it
+    builds without that parent, as before #616. Only a prerequisite of the dependent's own
+    ``(repo, base)`` target counts: a line is per target (#187), so none could carry
+    another target's into that base, and that dependent builds as it always has.
+
+    Each such prerequisite that is COMPLETE and that the fold would carry (a patch and a
+    usable target: :func:`integrate._fold_candidates`, the fold's own definition) is
+    judged once, however many bundles depend on it — its PR's state asked FIRST
+    (``merged.pr_state``), so a merged one never holds a dependent:
+
+    * **merged** — nothing to do: its work is already the base;
+    * **carry** — its branch is on record (:func:`integrate.unpublished`), that record is
+      not older than its latest sign-off (:func:`_record_predates_signoff`) and its PR is
+      open; the pre-wave fold merges that branch onto the line, as the in-run fold does
+      (#593);
+    * a **hold** (:data:`_HOLDS`) — the line must not carry it: :data:`_UNPUBLISHED`, no
+      branch on record, so nothing of it to fold; :data:`_STALE`, a record older than its
+      latest sign-off — an iterate keeps an earlier attempt's record (#593), so its branch
+      may be the rejected attempt's; :data:`_CLOSED`, its PR closed without merging, so the
+      line would put rejected work under every PR of its target; :data:`_NO_PR` or
+      :data:`_UNREAD`, no PR on record or a host that did not answer, so whether the base
+      already has its work is not known.
+
+    A dry-run asks no host and holds nothing: it plans the fold of each such prerequisite,
+    as the in-run dry fold plans each bundle as its would-be branch. One with no patch or
+    no target is never judged: its lack of work is the base.
+
+    Holds are worked out FIRST. A bundle is held when a prerequisite it would build on is
+    held — its ``Depends on`` ones and, when it would build on its target's line, its
+    ``Stacks on`` ones. A target gets a line only for a bundle that wants one (a ``Depends
+    on`` prerequisite to carry) and is not held, and a prerequisite is carried only for a
+    bundle that is not held: so a dependent held on one prerequisite starts no line for
+    another, and the rest of its target stays on the plain base. A prerequisite's own
+    prerequisites need no walk of their own: its branch was cut from the line it was built
+    on, so it carries them.
+
+    Returns the prerequisites to carry (bundle dirs, in name order) and the holds:
+    prerequisite name → ``(why, dependents)``, the drive-set bundles held on its account,
+    in drive-set order.
+
+    Read once, before wave 0, over the drive set as it then stands — the recovery children
+    adopted at ``k=-1`` included. A child a split adopts mid-run (:func:`_adopt_split_children`
+    after wave k) is not judged: an earlier run's prerequisite that it alone declares is
+    neither carried nor held (out of scope for #616)."""
+    def target(b: Path) -> tuple[str, str]:
+        # A COMPLETE bundle may have no brief.md left (#481): it names no target then.
+        return publish._resolve_target(b)[:2] if (b / "brief.md").exists() else ("", "")
+
+    verdicts: dict[str, str] = {}   # prerequisite bundle name → its verdict, judged once
+
+    def verdict(dep: str) -> str:
+        name = cfg.bundle(dep).name
+        if name not in verdicts:
+            p = cfg.find_bundle(dep)  # archived to completed/ too (#171)
+            if state.state(p) != state.COMPLETE or not integrate._fold_candidates([p]):
+                verdicts[name] = _BASE   # unfinished (`_runnable` holds it), or nothing to fold
+            elif dry:
+                verdicts[name] = _CARRY  # planned only: no host asked, nothing held
+            else:
+                pr = merged.pr_state(cfg, dep)
+                verdicts[name] = (_BASE if pr == "MERGED"
+                                  else _UNPUBLISHED if integrate.unpublished([p])
+                                  else _STALE if _record_predates_signoff(p)
+                                  else _CARRY if pr == "OPEN"
+                                  else _CLOSED if pr == "CLOSED"
+                                  else _UNREAD if _recorded_pr(p) else _NO_PR)
+        return verdicts[name]
+
+    def same_target(ids: list[str], tgt: tuple[str, str], gated: set[str]) -> list[str]:
+        # Out of the batch, not a `Depends on (merged)` edge, and of the dependent's target.
+        return [x for x in dict.fromkeys(ids) if cfg.bundle(x).name not in batch_names
+                and x not in gated and target(cfg.find_bundle(x)) == tgt]
