+    """Fold ``to_fold`` onto this run's integration line(s) — the ONE fold step of a
+    stack-mode run, shared by the fold after each wave (#593) and the pre-wave fold of
+    earlier runs' prerequisites (#616), so every fold of a run lands on the same per-batch
+    line (``batch``, #591) and continues it append-only.
+
+    Each target's pushed tip goes into ``folded_tips`` at once, before any re-gate: the
+    next fold continues from exactly that tip and refuses a line another run moved (#593).
+    A dry-run pushes nothing (None). ONE lock scope covers fold AND re-gate (#297 review
+    round 10): the locks stack keeps every target's integ lock held between the two, so no
+    gap exists in which another flow's publish-boundary sweep could remove the tree — or
+    another fold rewrite it — before the re-gate attests it. The optional re-gate
+    (#wave-model) validates EACH folded combination over its tip before a wave builds on
+    it; ``hold_lock=False``, as the stack already holds this tree's lock.
+
+    Returns what :func:`integrate.fold` returned, or None when the run must STOP: the fold
+    raised :class:`integrate.IntegrationError`, or a re-gate is red — each named on stderr
+    as ``what`` and ``then`` (what the stop leaves undone)."""
